/build/
# ...and any nested one. The rule above is anchored to the root, so `src/porthole/build/`
# was not covered and a 16 KB x86-64 ELF was staged from it. The subtree builds itself with
# its own Makefile, which is the whole point of it - so it makes its own build directory.
build/
*.o
*.elf
*.a

# Rust tooling build output. The glob is not decoration: `/tool/target/` alone missed
# `/tool/target-win/`, and 381 MB of `.pdb`, `.rlib` and `.exe` staged unnoticed because
# the pattern named one directory rather than the shape of the name cargo generates.
/tool/target*/

# Extracted reports from emulator runs. Not build/, because that directory is created by
# the VM that mounts this repository and can end up unwritable from the host.
/reports/

# The host build writes its framebuffer here when OBSCENE_DISPLAY_PNG is unset. Six
# megabytes of it sat at the repository root because nothing covered it.
/display.png
*.png
# ...except the loader screenshots, which are evidence rather than build output. They are
# small, they change only when a loader's behaviour does, and they are the only report two
# of the loaders produce at all.
!docs/screenshots/*.png
# ...and the logo, which the README embeds. The blanket above swallowed it, so the front
# page of this repository would have rendered a broken image from the first push - the
# `.ico` and `.svg` beside it were tracked, which is what made the gap invisible.
!assets/logo.png

# Mount litter. Deleting a file that is still open over the VM's 9p mount leaves one of
# these behind, hidden by the leading dot and invisible to `ls`. Regenerating the shaders
# had accumulated 133 of them in src/shaders, half a megabyte, none of it visible without
# looking for it.
.fuse_hidden*

# A report written to the repository root rather than into reports/. Three megabytes, and
# the only file in the root that nothing covered.
/obscene-report.txt

# Emulator litter. Created in the working directory by loaders run from here, and
# nothing to do with this project.
/_DownloadData/
/_TempData/
/_Textures/
# No `__pycache__/` or `*.pyc` rule, deliberately. There is no Python in this repository and
# there is not meant to be - the checks and the build scripts are shell. An ignore rule for
# bytecode is a quiet accommodation for a language that is not allowed here: it would hide the
# first stray file rather than let `git status` show it.

# Personal, per-machine permission grants — not shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Packages, wherever they land. `/titles/` below covers the ones kept deliberately; this
# covers the ones that accumulate at the repository root and were covered by nothing.
#
# Both kinds are here and neither belongs in history. `obscene.pkg` and `obscene-t.pkg` are
# this project's own build output, regenerated by `make pkg`. The rest are derivation input
# or comparisons against it - `real-item.pkg` and the `one-*`/`trunc*`/`tamper`/`flip`/
# `bisect` files carry a vendor content id rather than `OBSC00001`, which makes them exactly
# the material CLAUDE.md principle 1 bans from this repository.
#
# 350 MB of it was staged-ready at the root because the ban was written down and nothing
# enforced it. Keep working copies outside the tree, the way the scripts in `scripts/`
# already do - they read `$HOME`, not here.
*.pkg

# Vulkan's on-disk shader cache. Build output of whatever ran last, not of this project.
vulkan_pipeline_cache.bin

# Vendor containers used as derivation input, and never tracked.
#
# Same arrangement the NID chain already runs on: `obscene-tool mine` reads extracted
# firmware trees from outside the repository and writes a provenance-headed text file into
# `data/`, and the binaries it read stay where they were. `data/mined-names.txt` carries the
# exact commits and firmware versions it came from, which is what makes the derivation
# checkable by somebody who does not have the inputs.
#
# The packages here serve the same role for the container format: they are what a derivation
# is taken *from* and what a builder's output is checked *against*, never something the build
# depends on. Nothing in `tool/` may read this directory — generators read `data/`.
/titles/

# Packages: build output exactly like the *.elf above, and they piled up at the root because
# *.elf was covered and *.pkg never was - build-{full,min,stage1,stage2,sweep}.pkg, obscene*.pkg,
# real-item.pkg, all regenerable by `make`/bin/build-pkg.sh.
*.pkg

# Timestamped report copies. `/obscene-report.txt` caught the fixed name at the root; a run that
# stamps it (obscene-report-<epoch>.txt) walked straight past, thirteen of them at once.
obscene-report-*.txt

# The host GPU backend's pipeline cache, written beside a run and nothing to do with the source.
vulkan_pipeline_cache.bin

# A run's captured stdout, dumped at the root. It was even committed once (removed); this keeps it out.
/stdout.txt

# Whatever the person editing this happens to run. None of it is anybody else's business,
# and every one of these has been committed to some repository by accident at least once.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
